Description: An unofficial R client for self-hosted 'SeaTable' servers
    and for reading and writing 'SeaTable' data files directly. Reads a
    local '.dtable' export with no server at all, and talks to a
    self-hosted server over its REST (representational state transfer)
    application programming interface (API), returning tables, rows,
    columns and views as tidy 'tibble' objects through a
    column-type-aware coercion layer. Includes helpers for managing
    bases and files, converters to and from spreadsheet formats, and an
    optional 'shiny' explorer for interactive inspection. The 'SeaTable'
    API is documented at <https://api.seatable.com/>. This is an
    independent, third-party client: it is not affiliated with, endorsed
    by, or otherwise connected to SeaTable GmbH, and 'SeaTable' is their
    trademark, used here only to identify the software the package
    works with.
